# TDD REFACTOR PHASE SKILL

## Goal
Improve internal structure WITHOUT changing observable behavior.

---

## Input
- Passing production code
- Passing tests

---

## Output
- Same behavior
- Improved architecture and code structure

---

# Core Principle

Refactoring MUST move the code closer to:

✔ Clean Architecture  
✔ OOP service-based design  
✔ Explicit dependency injection  
✔ Domain-driven separation of concerns  

---

# Strict Rules

## Behavior Preservation Rule (CRITICAL)

- MUST NOT change observable behavior
- MUST NOT modify tests
- MUST NOT alter inputs/outputs

---

## Architecture Enforcement Rule (IMPORTANT)

Refactoring MUST preserve or improve:

### ✔ OOP Structure
- Business logic SHOULD live inside service classes
- Classes SHOULD represent domain/application responsibilities
- Functions SHOULD NOT replace service boundaries
- Services SHOULD encapsulate a single responsibility

---

### ✔ Dependency Injection Rule (STRICT)

- All dependencies MUST be injected via constructor
- No direct instantiation of infrastructure inside business logic
- No hidden dependency creation inside classes

✔ GOOD:
```ts
class UserService {
  constructor(private repo: UserRepository) {}
}